{"kind":"scout_result","runId":"0mtdp6imo-b17dfe3caa5272df","selected":[".squad/plan-lessons.md","api/src/features/identity/index.js","api/src/features/identity/identity.routes.js","api/src/features/identity/identity.service.js","api/src/features/identity/identity.repository.js","api/src/features/identity/identity.rules.js","api/src/platform/http/pagination.js","api/src/platform/http/permission.js","api/src/platform/http/errors.js","api/src/platform/db/migrations/0001__customers.sql","api/src/platform/db/connection.js","api/src/features/identity/identity.test.js","api/src/features/identity/accounts.test.js","api/src/platform/http/pagination.test.js","api/src/platform/http/errors.test.js","scripts/verify-architecture.mjs","api/src/app.js","api/openapi.json","docs/architecture.md"],"reasoning":"This story is the first non-identity feature and must follow the `identity` pattern exactly: public `index.js`, routes handling only req/res, service handling business logic, repository handling SQL exclusively, and rules handling validation. The intake explicitly warns that `scripts/verify-architecture.mjs` will reject any deviation (no req/res outside routes, no SQL outside repository, no feature reaching past another feature's index). \n\nThe drafter must read plan-lessons.md first per standing instructions. The five identity files form the mandatory architectural reference. Pagination.js is critical—the story must reuse readPagination (not write a second pager) to return `{ items, total, limit, offset }`. Permission.js shows how requireSubject() middleware enforces that any signed-in staff can search. Errors.js and errors.test.js establish error shape and testing patterns. The customers table schema comes from migration 0001. Connection.js shows parameterized query patterns (user input in search terms must be bound, never interpolated, with `%` and `_` treated as literals). \n\nBoth test patterns (identity.test.js and accounts.test.js) show how to structure route and service tests; pagination.test.js and errors.test.js show the patterns for those subsystems. The verify-architecture.mjs script is the gate before commit. App.js shows how features are mounted. Openapi.json may need the new search endpoint added. Docs/architecture.md provides context on layers.\n\nThe intake highlights four concrete decisions: phone normalization (explicitly decide: normalize or document limitation), soft-deleted exclusion (handled in SQL), empty results on no match (not a 404), and stable sort order choice. None of these require new files; they are implementation choices within the pattern already understood by studying identity and the platform pieces."}
